@@ -42,6 +42,18 @@ app.use(async (event) => {
 >
 > The examples below use a hardcoded value so they stay readable, but in a real app load a randomly generated secret of at least 32 characters from an environment variable such as `process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD`, and never commit it to source control. A guessable passphrase (even one ≥32 characters) is not safe.
 
+### Rotating the password
+
+To change the password without signing everyone out, pass a list with the new password first and the old one after it:
+
+```ts
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_NEW!, process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD!],
+});
+```
+
+The first password seals every session; the others are only used to open sessions sealed earlier. A session opened with an older password is resealed with the first one on its next cookie request. Remove the old password once the sessions sealed with it have expired, and keep the list short: an invalid session costs a key derivation for each password.
+
 This will initialize a session and return an header `Set-Cookie` with a cookie named `h3` and an encrypted content.
 
 If the request contains a cookie named `h3` or a header named `x-h3-session`, the session will be initialized with the content of the cookie or the header.
